# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini API
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Injected at runtime from the deployment platform's secret store.
# Configure this in the Secrets / Environment Variables panel of your host
# (Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables).
# Never commit a real key.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ask Atlas providers (server-side failover chain)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only keys. Never add a VITE_ prefix: these must stay out of the
# browser bundle. The chain falls over to the next provider when one is
# rate limited or down.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY="sk-or-v1-..."
# NVIDIA_API_KEY="nvapi-..."
# ASK_AI_ORDER="gemini,openrouter,nvidia"

# Optional N-ATLAS slot. When NATLAS_BASE_URL is set, N-ATLAS is prepended
# to the chain; otherwise the slot is skipped silently. NATLAS_API_KEY is
# optional (public gateways may not need one).
# NATLAS_BASE_URL="https://..."
# NATLAS_API_KEY=""
# NATLAS_MODEL="NCAIR1/N-ATLaS"
# Reference self-hosted setup: docs/local-inference.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NIPOST Digital Postcode API (NDAPS)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
#
# The app never calls api.postcode.gov.ng from the browser. Every NDAPS request
# goes through the server-side proxy in `src/server/nipost/handler.ts`
# (`/api/nipost/*`), shared by the Vite dev middleware and the Vercel Function.
# That is why these are server-only: the publishable key is locked to an origin
# allowlist, so a browser call is rejected with `origin_not_allowed`, while a
# server call carries no browser Origin and is served. The key therefore stays
# out of the shipped bundle. Never add a VITE_ prefix to either variable.
#
# `npm run dataset` reads the same two variables through Vite's loadEnv.

NIPOST_API_BASE_URL="https://api.postcode.gov.ng"
NIPOST_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="nipost_pk_your_publishable_key_here"